    "description": "Silver Holdco JV, LLC was the 50/50 Macquarie Infrastructure Partners V and Medical Properties Trust lessor partnership for eight Steward-operated Massachusetts hospitals. The approximately US$1.7bn portfolio closed on March 14, 2022 under long-term triple-net leases. Steward's 2024 bankruptcy ended the lease economics, and Macquarie and Medical Properties Trust surrendered the collateral and cash to Apollo-managed lenders in exchange for debt releases. Five hospitals were subsequently sold, St. Elizabeth's transferred to Massachusetts, and Carney and Nashoba remained in a separate lender workout vehicle. The original Silver Holdco platform is therefore realized from 2024; successor operators, government transferees, individual property SPVs and the lender workout pool are not counted as successor PortCos.",
